VNA Hanoi - VNA correspondents reported that on the morning of February 11, Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife visited the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD, short for "Brunei Darussalam University") during their visit to Brunei Darussalam.
The University of Brunei Darussalam is the largest higher education and scientific research center in Brunei, ranking third in the regional university rankings.
The University of Brunei Darussalam is one of the symbols of Vietnam-Brunei cooperation in education and training.
The University of Brunei Darussalam officially established a cooperation relationship with Vietnam's FPT University in July 2013, mainly in the field of English training.
In addition to English, French, German, Japanese, and Korean, the University of Brunei Darussalam has also included Vietnamese in its curriculum.
During the visit to the University of Brunei Darussalam, the Prime Minister of Vietnam Nguyen Tan Dung and his wife had an exchange with students of Vietnamese language class.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh is happy that more and more foreigners are learning Vietnamese, and he will actively contribute to promoting the image of Vietnamese culture and local characteristics to the world.
The Prime Minister of the Government, Pheung Amnim, expressed his belief and hope that the Vietnamese language teacher team of University of Brunei Darussalam would become stronger and stronger; the students of Vietnamese class would be more and more interested in Vietnamese language, and would strive to learn it fluently as soon as possible, and become the messenger of the friendly cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also took the opportunity to communicate with Vietnamese students studying English at FPT-UBD Global Center in Chanh Muong District, Quang Nam Province, via video, to learn about their learning situation, especially during the pandemic.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Tan Dung, believed that the cooperation relationship between Vietnam FPT University and Brunei University, especially the FPT-UBD Global Center, was a vivid symbol of the cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei in education.
At the same time, we hope that the students of the center will make greater progress in their studies and make positive contributions to the friendly and cooperative relations between Vietnam and the two countries.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly appreciated the achievements of the two countries in education cooperation during his discussions with the Minister of Education of Brunei and leaders of Brunei University. These achievements include the cooperation between FPT University and Brunei University, as well as the initiative of Brunei University to include Vietnamese language in the teaching curriculum.
Prime Minister Lim Jong-hyeon hopes that the University of Brunei Darussalam will continue to pay attention to ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and further expand the scale of Vietnamese language classes.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Tan Dung, also highly evaluated the positive effects of cooperation between the two countries on the basis of the Memorandum of Understanding on Educational Cooperation signed in April 2014; he suggested that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively carry out various short-term exchange training projects, such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly praised the establishment of the first branch of the University of Brunei in Vietnam in Southeast Asia; believing that the university will grow in scale in the region and the world; and further expanding cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
At the same time, Premier Fan Mingqiang and his wife planted a commemorative tree in the campus of the University of Brunei Darussalam and left a message in the commemorative book.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh wished that the University of Brunei Darussalam would continue to develop and contribute more and more to the education sector of Brunei. He also hoped that the cooperation between Vietnamese education and training institutions and Brunei would become more extensive and deeper.
(Finish)
Vietnam News Agency
“Important Engine of Global Recovery” - chinanews.com
“In response to the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic, China’s economy has shown great resilience.
Recently, the market expectations show that the international community generally looks forward to China's future development.
“Hugo Rios, a well-known Chinese issues expert in Spain and honorary advisor of China Policy Observation Network, recently said in an interview with this newspaper that China’s epidemic prevention and control has entered a new stage, and the vitality of economic and social development will be further released.
Rio said that China has demonstrated its economic resilience and management level by effectively responding to various unexpected factors with its outstanding economic governance experience and measures, which fully reflects its economic vitality.
At the same time, China is firmly committed to expanding its opening up to the outside world, and the internal driving force of economic development is constantly strengthened, and state-owned enterprises and private enterprises are developing together.
Every year, the two sessions of the National People's Congress of China are held, and the delegates discuss the national development plans and hot issues of the people's livelihood, and widely consolidate consensus, consolidate the hearts and minds, and add power to the development of China.
“Since the reform and opening up, China has achieved long-term high-speed development, and has now entered the stage of high-quality development.
The international community is looking forward to China's wisdom and China's plan, and is looking forward to China's development to bring new opportunities to the world.
"Li said that China is currently making every effort to promote scientific and technological innovation, inject new impetus into economic and social development, and "investment, talent training, and policy incentives have made China continue to be full of vitality in the new five-year plan,"" he said.
To Rios, economic reform is a daunting task for any country.
Under the leadership of the Communist Party of China, China has played the advantages of market economy and the superiority of socialist system, and taken proactive and positive measures to stabilize the economy.
Around the strategic base of expanding domestic demand, China will strengthen financial support for the real economy, support the development of private enterprises, small and medium-sized enterprises and manufacturing industry, insist on innovative development, promote employment, improve the income and living standards of the Chinese people, and meet the diverse and multi-layered consumption needs of the people. China will fully, accurately and comprehensively implement the new development concept, focus on promoting high-quality development, build a new development pattern, and bring more growth opportunities to the world.
This year is the 10th anniversary of the proposal of the Belt and Road Initiative.
