Several indicators of decline in Taiwan's economy in the first quarter of the year - China News
Xinhua News Agency, Taipei, February 11 (reported by Zhao Bo and Huang Yang) - The export trade volume "连五黑" and the manufacturing purchasing managers index (PMI) have been contracting for seven consecutive months, and the consumer price index (CPI) has seen "3-digit" again... Recently, the Taiwan authority released the economic data of January 2023.
Experts analyzed that the performance of the Taiwanese economy at the beginning of the year was not good, and the growth pressure was not small.
According to the Taiwan authorities’ department in charge of financial affairs, the region’s exports amounted to US$31.51 billion in January this year, a year-on-year decrease of 21.2%, and the fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The export value of 11 major export commodities fell year-on-year in the same period.
The plastic rubber and its products and optical instruments fell the most, with a year-on-year decrease of 37.6% and 35.7% respectively.
The export of electronic components fell by 20.1% year-on-year, the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, the annual decline of integrated circuits was 18.3%, creating the largest decline in 14 years.
Chai Mianna, the head of the Statistics Department, said that this showed that the weak demand for consumer electronics had spread, and the electronic industry was entering a correction period.
Statistics show that in January, both imports and exports of Taiwan region fell, and the excess amount of exports was only 2.34 billion US dollars, which is the lowest level in the past three years.
The Financial Supervisory Service of the Taiwan authorities believes that the global terminal demand is reduced, and the adjustment of industrial inventory has inhibited the willingness of manufacturers to purchase raw materials. The export slump is unlikely to improve in the short term. The export decline of Taiwan in the first quarter of this year is expected to be worse than expected.
According to the Taiwan China Economic Research Institute, the seasonally adjusted Taiwan Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index (PMI) in January was 40.4%, a decrease of 3.3 percentage points from December last year, and contracted for seven consecutive months.
In the economic monitoring indicator system, the PMI is 50% as the demarcation line of prosperity and decline, and the index is greater than 50%, which represents prosperity expansion, and vice versa for contraction.
In January, the five components of the PMI in Taiwan were tightened, including new orders, production and employment, and the delivery time of suppliers was shortened, and the inventory was tightened.
All six industries have a contracted PMI, and the industries are ranked in order of the contraction speed, namely, the electrical and mechanical equipment industry (35.1%), the electronic and optical industry (35.2%), the chemical and biotechnology and medical industry (39.2%), the basic raw material industry (42.4%), the transportation equipment industry (42.6%), and the food and textile industry (45.7%).
In terms of prices, the “Directorate-General of Budget, Accounting and Statistics” of the Taiwan authorities announced that the CPI of Taiwan in January this year was 3.04%, which exceeded 3% for the first time since July last year.
Among them, the price of vegetables soared by 28.25%, creating a new high in 17 months.
The special member of the Executive Yuan of Taiwan, Cao Zhigang, admitted that the increase in vegetable prices exceeded expectations. Excluding the factor of the Spring Festival, the average CPI in January and February of this year should be close to 2.71% in December of last year, and the inflation pressure is still there, and it is still at a high point.
Looking forward to this year's Taiwan economy, experts expressed pessimism after comprehensive reports by local media such as United Daily News and Yahoo Finance.
According to analysis by Wu Daoren, a professor at the “Central University” Economics Department, the decline in exports may cause problems with cash flow for export manufacturers, and the risk of debt default will increase.
At the same time, the reduction of orders leads to the reduction of labor costs of manufacturers, which affects the labor market and the family economy, and in turn, it affects the consumption capacity.
Chiou Tsa-sheng, a researcher at the Institute of Taiwanese Economic Research, believes that the inflationary situation in Europe and the United States has not been resolved, and the demand continues to shrink. He predicts that the export decline in Taiwan will continue until the first half of the year.
Due to the fact that Taiwan's economy is supported by exports, and affected by the low exports, the economic growth performance of the whole year will be worse than that of last year.
Does the balloon incident make America look better?
Strengthening restrictions on technology exports to China
The Wall Street Journal reported today that the United States is preparing to further tighten the export of technology to China after the balloon incident.
The current and former security officials said the balloon incident highlighted the national security threat posed by China and would help to win more political support for strengthening U.S. technology protection.
The United States said that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence gathering and communication.
According to Martijn Rasser, a senior official of the former US Central Intelligence Agency and now serving at the New American Security Center in Washington, D.C.
"This is undoubtedly adding fuel to the fire and supports the hard-line view against China."
White House press secretary Karine Jean-Pierre said on Thursday that “we will also consider taking more extensive action to expose and respond to China’s larger-scale surveillance activities, which pose a threat to our national security and to our allies and partners.
“US officials said they had informed the governments of more than 30 countries about the balloon incident, and international coordination is crucial to counter the Chinese threat. ”
According to Emily Benso, a senior research fellow at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, in addition to the actions of the Biden administration, the newly established Select Committee on Strategic Competition between the United States and the Chinese Communist Party in the US House of Representatives may also put pressure on the United States to take more stringent measures to slow down China’s development.
She said that members of Congress would feel increasing pressure to take a more hardline stance, which could force the White House to take a more hardline stance.
The Wall Street Journal reported that many advocates of stricter export controls are also pushing to expand the scope of the controls to include artificial intelligence and other industries.
The US government is also in the process of developing an investment review plan to assess whether there are potential national security threats from China to its overseas investments.
Analysts say the White House may face pressure to move faster on the plan.
First batch of personal pension products launched for sale, with the shortest holding period of only 360 days - chinanews.com
The first individual pension products have been launched.
7 products of the family institution can be selected, the shortest holding period is only 360 days
Personal pension products have finally been launched.
On February 10th, the China Wealth Management Network released the list of the first batch of individual pension product offerings from Industrial and Commercial Bank of China (ICBC), Agricultural Bank of China (ABC), and Postal Savings Bank of China (PSBC). Seven ICBC-managed individual pension products have officially launched.
At this point, the "shelves" of the personal pension account are finally full of four types of products: personal pension savings, personal pension investment, personal pension insurance, and publicly offered mutual funds.
It is introduced that the first batch of personal pension wealth management products are all publicly offered net value open-end products, including 5 newly issued products and 2 existing products, except for one product which is a mixed type product, the other 6 products are fixed income type products.
The Beijing Youth Daily reporters found that 4 out of the 5 new products were from ICBC Wealth Management, all of which were fixed income products, and the shortest holding period was 365 days, 540 days, 720 days, and 1080 days, respectively, and the corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90%, and 5.25% - 5.75%.
The remaining new product is "Postal Savings Wealth Add Yi Heng Hongjing Shortest Holding Period 1095 Days 1 ", which is also a fixed income product. It started collecting on February 10 and ended on February 19. The risk level is level 2.
One of the two existing products is Agricultural Bank of China Wealth Management “Agricultural Bank of China Unity·Spiritual” 360-day Science and Technology Innovation RMB Wealth Management Product, which is a mixed type investment product with a risk level of three.
Another product that is still available is "Postal Savings Wealth Additional Yinhe Hongjin Minimum Holding Period 365 Days No. 1," a fixed income product. It started collecting funds on December 30 last year and officially started operating on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net value on February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the "Opinions on Promoting the Development of Individual Pension Insurance" issued by the Office of the State Council, the financial products that the personal pension fund account funds can invest in include bank wealth management products, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, publicly offered funds, etc.
The first batch of individual pension fund management products was launched, marking that individual pension investors can officially purchase investment products through the individual pension fund account.
In November last year, the China Insurance Regulatory and Supervisory Commission formulated the “Interim Measures for the Management of Individual Pension Business of Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies”.
The Regulations provide that participants can purchase personal pension savings, personal pension wealth management products, personal pension insurance products, and personal pension open-end fund products through their individual pension funds accounts.
Subsequently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Administration of Taxation issued a notice to clarify that the individual pension plan will be implemented in 36 pilot cities and regions, including Beijing, Tianjin, and Hebei Shijiazhuang and the Xiongan New Area, Shanxi Jincheng City, and other cities and regions.
As of the end of 2022, the number of participants in personal pensions was 19.54 million, and the number of contributors was 6.13 million, with a total contribution amount of 14.2 billion yuan.
Previously, participating banks had only introduced three products for pilot testing: individual pension savings, individual pension insurance, and individual public offering funds.
Now that a variety of personal pension wealth management products have gathered together, how should investors choose?
According to experts from the product development department of ICBC Credit, compared with other personal pension products, the pilot period of the pension wealth management products and personal pension wealth management products have three characteristics.
One is prudence, the risk management mechanism is more complete, the investment strategy and concept are more prudent, and the third-party independent custody is implemented.
Secondly, it is long-term. The term of the pilot period of the long-term care finance products is 5 years and above. In the next step, the holding period of the individual pension finance products will be 1 year as a principle, and it will be encouraged to hold for 3 years or more.
Third, it is inclusive. The threshold for purchasing products is low, and the starting point is generally 1 yuan, and some are as low as 0.01 yuan. The fees such as custody fees and management fees are more favorable.
Professionals pointed out that investors should choose according to the characteristics of the product and their risk tolerance.
The personal pension savings have the characteristics of long-term, high interest rate and high safety, suitable for people with low risk tolerance; personal pension insurance products focus on protection, suitable for people who cannot bear investment risks and can accept stable returns; while personal pension investment products and publicly offered funds do not guarantee the principal or returns, have certain investment risks, but have high expected returns, suitable for people with certain financial knowledge and high risk tolerance.
Written by reporters of Beijing News, Cheng Yi, and coordinated by Qiu Hai Bo.
The Central Committee members, Standing Committee members and leading cadres of the provincial level or above learned the essence of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress at the seminar on studying and implementing the essence of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress - Rolling News - Hunan Daily - Huanxi
The Central Committee of the CPC, the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, and the leading cadres of the provincial and ministerial level studied and implemented the essence of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress.
February 11, 2023 at 1:07 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large | medium | small】
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 (covering the afternoon) - The study of the 20th CPC National Congress and the 20th CPC National Congress on the implementation of the new era of socialism with Chinese characteristics and the new members of the Central Committee, the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, the leading cadres of the provincial-level departments and the leading cadres of the ministries and commissions attended the closing ceremony of the study of the implementation of the new era of socialism with Chinese characteristics and the 20th CPC National Congress in the Central Party School (the National Academy of Public Administration) on the 10th. Xi Jinping, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and the Secretary of the Central Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee, made a summary speech.
He said that we should deeply study and implement the important spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's speech at the opening ceremony of the seminar, more firmly embrace the "two establishments", resolutely do the "two safeguards", enhance our capabilities, and work hard to push forward all aspects of Chinese-style modernization, and create a performance that can stand the test of history, practice and people in the process of building a socialist modernized country in all respects and promoting the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all the students were guided by the thoughts of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics, and carefully studied the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and the important speech of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar. They conducted in-depth research and exchanges on a series of major theoretical and practical issues of Chinese-style modernization, deepened their understanding of these issues, and strengthened their confidence and determination in comprehensively promoting Chinese-style modernization under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee with Xi Jinping as the core, and their sense of responsibility and mission in fulfilling their duties and responsibilities, ensuring a good start for the new journey in the new era.
At the graduation ceremony, 10 representatives of the seminar made speeches to report and share their learning achievements.
Cai Qi said that learning and implementing the thoughts of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress is both the primary political task of the present and the future, and a long-term strategic task. It is necessary to promote learning and implementation in-depth, thorough and sincere, in accordance with the requirements of "comprehensive learning, comprehensive understanding, and comprehensive implementation".
To understand more profoundly the decisive significance of the “two establishments”, to firmly safeguard the core position of General Secretary Xi Jinping, to safeguard the authority of the Party Central Committee and the centralized and unified leadership, to continuously improve political judgment, political understanding and political execution, and to always maintain high consistency with the Party Central Committee with Xi Jinping as the core in thoughts, politics and actions.
We should strive to master the basic skills of Marxist theory, consciously use the innovative theory of the Party to arm our minds, guide our practice and promote our work, and work hard in deep study, profound understanding and sincere practice, so as to truly learn with firm belief, learn with absolute loyalty and learn with a sense of mission and responsibility.
To earnestly implement all decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with an enterprising spirit, advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves to work hard, get down to business as a good “construction supervisor”, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
We must remember that comprehensive strict Party discipline is a never-ending journey, and the self-revolution of the Party is a never-ending journey. We must bear the political responsibility of comprehensive strict Party discipline, and focus on the political construction of the Party, and deepen the new great cause of building the Party in the new era.
To strengthen the ability to drive high-quality development, serve the people, and prevent and resolve risks, we should vigorously develop the spirit of investigation and research, and resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucratism.
Stone Tiefeng, Li Ganjie, Li Shuyan, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jingguo, and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony and Chen Xi presided over the graduation ceremony.
East Germany's last communist prime minister dies
The successor of the East German Communist Party reported in a statement that “Last night, Hans Modrow left us at the age of 95.
Therefore, our party has lost an important leader.
“
On November 13, 1989, four days after the opening of the Berlin Wall, which separated East Berlin and West Berlin for 28 years, Modrow said he would help turn East Germany into a democratic country.
At that time, because of protests in East Germany demanding democracy and freedom, communist leaders were forced to resign.
After Gorbachev took over in the Soviet Union, he called for changes in the Soviet-dominated Eastern Europe.
In March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free election in the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The election results led to him no longer serving as Prime Minister.
Despite Mordor's reforms, opponents accused him of trying to delay the political changes and reunification that took place in October 1990.
He has also been criticized for attempting to reform rather than abolish the secret police.
In 1993, Mordell was found guilty of electoral fraud in the 1989 municipal elections, but did not go to jail.
Some have charged that these charges were motivated by political considerations.
From 1990 to 1994, Mödrath continued to serve in the German Parliament, and from 1999 to 2004, he served as a member of the European Parliament.
Modero sees himself as a reformer and hopes to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want the old East Germany to return, but said that the achievements of East Germany should be recognized.
Mordor was born in 1928 in the German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica in Poland) and received training as a machinist.
During World War II, he served as a platoon leader in the youth fire brigade and, as the conflict drew to a close, became a member of the Nazi militia organization, the Volkssturm, which conscripted men aged 16 to 60 for the final struggle of the war.
When he was 17, Modrow was captured by the Soviet army and taken as a prisoner of war to the Soviet Union, where he took part in anti-fascist courses and became a staunch communist.
In 1949, the year East Germany was founded, he returned to the country and found a job as a mechanical engineer and continued his studies in social sciences and economics, earning a doctorate.
Modrow was a staff member of the Free German Youth movement, which almost all East German young people joined, and rose to become the chairman of the party in the Dresden region between 1973 and 1989 through the ruling Socialist Unity Party (SED).
He has also been a member of the East German parliament for more than 30 years.
In 1990, Modrow became the de facto leader of East Germany and held the highest state office.
VNA Hanoi – VNA correspondent for Vietnam’s Prime Minister Nguyen Xuan Phuc and his wife have successfully completed their official visit to Singapore and Brunei, achieving comprehensive, practical, and specific results.
In the three days of his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Feng Mingping attended more than 30 different events.
The achievements have injected new impetus into the development of the strategic partnership and comprehensive partnership between Vietnam and New Zealand in a more profound, more comprehensive and effective direction.
During the visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh continued to reiterate the foreign policy line of the Party and the State of Vietnam, namely independence, diversity, and variability, and the willingness to be a good friend and reliable partner of all countries, as well as a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is the need of their respective countries, and they are committed to promoting the well-being of their people and to peace, stability and development in the region and the world.
At the meetings and talks, Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister, agreed with the leaders of Singapore and Brunei to continue to strengthen political trust with Vietnam through the high-level delegation visits, effective implementation of the various bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
During the meeting with business leaders, the symposium or the attendance of the economic forum, Prime Minister Pham Minh Mẫn emphasized that Vietnam welcomed and created favorable conditions for Singaporean and Bruneian enterprises to expand investment in digital transformation, green energy, high technology, innovation and creativity in Vietnam.
This visit will not only help deepen the cooperation between Vietnam, Singapore and Brunei in various traditional fields such as politics, foreign affairs, economy, security, national defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, and people-to-people exchanges, but also create a cooperation framework for the two countries in new potential fields such as digital economy, green economy, energy transformation, innovation and creativity, smart city, and sustainable development.
King of Brunei Hassanal Bolkiah and Prime Minister of Viet Nam Pham Minh Chinh are preparing to enter the bilateral meeting.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
During his visits to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh arranged time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of the Vietnamese diaspora living in the two countries.
At the meeting with the leaders of the two countries, Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam, suggested that the authorities of both countries pay more attention to the fair treatment of the Vietnamese people in the host country, create conditions for the local Vietnamese community to contribute to the local society, and create favorable conditions for the development of bilateral relations.
The proposal has been agreed to and supported by both leaders of the two countries.
In particular, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also shared with leaders of the two countries the desire for a united, peaceful, stable and prosperous ASEAN community; and agreed to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN countries and enhance the central role of ASEAN in the regional and international context of complex and volatile.
Thanks to the important achievements, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh's official visit to Singapore and Brunei will contribute to effectively implementing the 13th National Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam's guidelines on prioritizing relations with neighboring countries in the new context, effectively implementing the 12th conclusion of the Politburo of the Communist Party of Vietnam on the situation of Vietnamese overseas workers in the new context (12-KL/TW), and making positive contributions to the national solidarity force.
(Finish)
NEWS GOV-MO: Police News Release: Police Department Warns of Scam Texts from Fake Telecommunications Companies
Recently, the Police have received a number of cases of telecommunication fraud. The fraudsters pretended to be the Hong Kong Telecommunications Company and sent the victim a fraudulent text message with a website link. They lured the victim to enter a fake website to redeem the reward, which was due to expire.
The victim followed the instructions to enter the credit card information and verification code, and then received a notification from the financial institution that there were unidentified records of consumption on the credit card. The victim suspected that the credit card information had been stolen from the above website.
After investigation, it was confirmed that the relevant telecommunications company did not send the above short message.
The Police Force appealed to the public to be vigilant if they received similar SMS messages, and not to click on the links or provide any personal information in the SMS; and to be extra careful if they were asked to provide credit card details, account transaction passwords and transaction verification codes, as they could be victims of credit card fraud.
Fraud Alert:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity information and improve personal prevention awareness.
2. Do not log in to websites with unknown origins and register your personal information and credit card information on the website, so as to avoid being stolen by others.
3. Beware of fake websites and phishing websites, and always pay attention to whether the website address is completely consistent with the official website.
4. Install antivirus software on your mobile phone, mobile device or computer and update it regularly.
If you suspect that you have been a victim of fraud or any other crime, please contact the Police Commissioner's Fraud Reporting Hotline at 8800 7777 or the Crime Report Line at 993 for assistance immediately.
EU summit struggles with refugee policy, EU officials: every step of the reception process is a bottleneck - chinanews.com
EU summit is in a dilemma over the refugee policy, and EU officials said that every step of the reception process has bottlenecks
【Global Times reporter in Belgium, Ni Ruifeng】According to the report of the French news agency on February 10, at the latest EU summit held that day, the President of the European Commission, von der Leyen, said that the leaders of the EU agreed to issue stricter policies on illegal immigration to make it easier to expel illegal immigrants.
The EU's move is reportedly in response to growing concerns about illegal immigration in Europe. Nowadays, the core problem of the EU is that the number of illegal immigrants who can be repatriated is very small.
According to the summit document, EU leaders called on the Commission to "immediately mobilize a large amount of EU funds" to strengthen external borders with infrastructure and surveillance.
However, the EU and its member states have been arguing over issues such as the payment of the fence.
Merkel has repeatedly said that EU funds will not pay for the costs.
But some diplomats from member countries said that if the EU could shoulder some of the cost of installing cameras, observation towers and other infrastructure along the external borders, it would free up national budgets to speed up construction.
The European Euractiv website said that EU officials admitted that every step of the refugee reception process was a bottleneck, and the limited reception capacity and the overburdened immigration authorities of member countries could not stop refugees from submitting "countless" asylum applications in EU countries, and the refugee reception system of the EU was in a "permanent crisis" near.
The European Commission estimated that the Schengen countries in the EU received more than 92,000 asylum applications last year, an increase of nearly half compared to the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded more than 330,000 illegal border crossings last year.
In this context, the summit also agreed on a "principle" that EU member states can deport illegal immigrants to their home countries based on a court ruling of another member state.
In addition, the report said that EU leaders also agreed to "increase the use of the concept of safe countries", which will pave the way for the EU to establish a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
The Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Xia Lijiang, visited China to convey the message of Song Tao: welcome the Green Party to visit China under the consensus of 92.
The Vice Chairman of the Chinese Nationalist Party in Taiwan, Shih Lien-jang, met with the Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, Song Tao, and the member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, Wang Meng.
Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor of the Nationalist Party’s official institution, the Guoguang Foundation, was interviewed by the Central News Agency of Taiwan yesterday evening. He actively praised Song Taizheng for his words to Xia Litian, saying that China welcomes Green Party people to visit the mainland as long as they acknowledge the “92 Consensus” and are against Taiwan independence.
The Nationalist Party considered it a new thing.
Xia Litian met with Song Tao earlier in the day, and the news did not mention this statement.
The ruling Democratic Progressive Party in Taiwan has been clarifying its refusal to accept the “92 Consensus.”
According to Central News Agency today, the delegation led by the Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Shali Lian, visited the mainland. During their stay in Beijing, they met with the member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee Wang Meng, the new Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, Song Tao, and the Secretary of the Beijing Municipal Committee, Yin Li.
Xia Litian and Song Tao talked about the political basis of the national government and the anti-Taiwan independence, and Zhao Chunshan, senior advisor of the National Party’s National Government Fund, said in the meeting that the National Party’s “nine-two consensus” is the original “nine-two consensus”.
Zhao Chunshan analyzed that this was different from the previous meetings in which he participated.
Recently, I had a video conference with scholars from the mainland, and this time, I did not hear any scholars talking about the unification and the “anti-secession law”. Instead, I heard the restoration of exchanges and dialogues.
Zhao Chunshan pointed out that the two sides were in a dangerous situation, and the mainland of China hoped to convey its intention to improve relations through the Kuomintang.
Because there is no mutual trust between the CPC and the DPP, the other party still wants to do a good job for the people of Taiwan, and the representative does not want to ruin the relationship between the two sides.
According to Zhao Chunshan, Wang Hongwen also personally gave instructions to Song Tao to tell "you must implement the requests made by them (Taiwanese farmers and fishermen)" and if it is not possible to solve it comprehensively, it should be handled on a case-by-case basis.
The report did not mention whether the KMT people mentioned the daily harassment of Chinese military aircraft and warships when visiting the mainland, the agricultural and fishery problems in a few counties and cities in Taiwan, and whether the reporter of Central Daily asked such questions.
What was "the object" that crashed in the airspace above阿拉斯加?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
The US military used the most advanced stealth fighter jet F-22 to shoot down an unidentified object flying in the sky of Alaska, USA, on Friday afternoon (February 10th).
The crash site is ten miles from the coast of Alaska.
This is the second time in less than a week that the U.S. military has shot down an unidentified flying object.
Last Saturday, a Chinese spy balloon was destroyed in the airspace of the United States near the coast of South Carolina in the United States after drifting for several days.
The Pentagon said the second object shot down entered US airspace over the north-east of Alaska on Thursday night and was tracked by the US military as it moved at an altitude of 12,000 metres (40,000 feet), about the size of a small car, much smaller than the previous Chinese spy balloon.
The Pentagon also believes that there is no evidence that the object is maneuverable.
The White House's National Security Council's strategic communications coordinator, John Coy, said on Friday that although the specific appearance of the flying object in the sky was unclear, it "posed a reasonable threat to the safety of civil aviation."
Kobe said that the object was different from the spy balloon found in the United States, which did not have a "payload" hanging from it.
Kobe said, "We call it an 'object' because it's the best description we can give it at this point."
Biden, who took advice from the Pentagon before ordering the strike, made the decision "very carefully," Cooke added.
The official description of the object by the United States can be roughly summarized as: the size is equivalent to that of a small car, it has no joystick and no suspension device, and the flight altitude is about 10,000 meters.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
There are many analysis and guesses on the Internet that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It may be the same as the spy balloon that invaded the US airspace and the Chinese balloon that floated in the air in Latin America, and they are all from China, and they are performing some tasks in different places.
Some have even linked the Alaska "object" to the mysterious flying object (UFO).
The report by the US Newsweek quoted a tweet posted by Peter Meijer, a former US Congressman, on Friday, saying, "I really hope that this 'unidentified flying object' is a spy balloon, rather than a legitimate UFO."
The irony of conflating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is striking, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, he said.
Meeks tweeted this shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
According to the news magazine, it is not just Mayer who is suspicious of the object being a UFO.
Tennessee Republican Congressman Tim Burchett criticized the government's cover-up of intelligence last month, and demanded the National Intelligence Directorate (DNI) to publish a report on "unidentified flying objects".
Xi Jinping's Letter to the Members of the Chinese Medical Team in Africa Encourages Them to Practice Compassionate Medicine to Benefit the Local People and to Tell the Story of China with Real Actions - News - Hunan Daily - Huanxi Shibao
Xi Jinping sent a letter of encouragement to the Chinese medical team in Africa, urging them to use their medical skills to help the local people and to tell the Chinese story with their deeds.
February 11, 2023 at 1:09 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large medium small】
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 - General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee, President of the People's Republic of China and Chairman of the Central Military Commission Xi Jinping sent a letter to the 19th batch of medical team to the Central African Republic on February 9, expressing his greetings to them and all the medical teams abroad and making a sincere wish.
In his reply, Xi Jinping said that you are white angels who save lives and heal wounds and friendly messengers who spread love, and you have overcome difficulties in work and life in China-Africa and served the local people with heart.
This year is the 60th anniversary of the dispatch of Chinese medical aid teams abroad. We would like to express our sincere condolences to those who are currently and have been carrying out medical aid missions abroad.
Xi Jinping pointed out that the Chinese people love peace and cherish life, and the foreign medical assistance is a vivid demonstration of this.
I hope that you will not forget your original intention and remember your mission, and vigorously carry forward the spirit of the Chinese medical team of not being afraid of hardship, being willing to make sacrifices, saving lives and treating injuries, and showing boundless love. Use your kindness and medical skills to benefit the local people, tell the Chinese story with practical actions, and make greater contributions to promoting the construction of a community with a shared future for mankind.
Foreign medical assistance is an important component of China's foreign aid work.
In 1963, China sent the first medical assistance team to Algeria.
Over the past 60 years, China has sent medical teams to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, the Americas, Europe and Oceania, with a total of 30,000 medical staff, providing medical services to 290 million people, and won widespread praise from the international community.
Currently, the medical team is working in 115 medical points in 56 countries around the world, and nearly half of them are in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th batch of the Chinese medical team to Africa wrote a letter to Xi Jinping, reporting on studying and implementing the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress, providing medical services to local residents, and expressing their determination to contribute to the construction of a community with a shared future for human health.
Iran marks revolution anniversary with hacking of president's TV speech
Iran held an official gathering on Saturday to commemorate the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ebrahim Raisi's televised speech.
The president's televised address was interrupted on the internet for about a minute, and a group of black hackers against the Iranian government appeared on the screen, whose name was "Edalat Ali (Ali Justice)".
There was also a voice shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic."
According to a report by Reuters today, Iranian hackers interrupted the state television station's coverage of the anniversary of the revolution.
Iran's hard-line government faced its boldest challenge yet from young protesters demanding its overthrow on the 44th anniversary of the Islamic Revolution, but President Hassan Rouhani called on "deceived youth" to repent so they can be pardoned by Iran's top leader.
Protests continue to sweep across Iran following the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini in custody of the country's morality police in September.
The deadly crackdown by Iranian security forces on protests is one of the most formidable challenges faced by the Islamic Republic since the 1979 revolution overthrew 2,500 years of monarchy.
As part of an amnesty in celebration of the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities freed Friday two political prisoners who had been on hunger strike: Farkhaddin Mesbah-Yazdi and Fariba Adel-Haeri, an Iranian-French scholar.
Earlier, the Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty decree, which includes some prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to the Human Rights Activists News Agency (HRANA), as of Friday, 528 protesters had been killed, including 71 minors.
The report also said that 70 government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
Iranian leaders and state media have been calling for a vote of confidence in Saturday's gathering to show opposition to the protests and support for the government for weeks.
On Friday night, the anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, official media showed fireworks as part of the government-sponsored celebrations, and people shouted "Allahu Akbar!
“(God is the greatest!)”
However, there is also much shouting in assemblies of “Dictator must die!”
and the 'death of the Islamic Republic' in videos posted on social media.
On Saturday, the government television station broadcasted live footage of the official gathering in all the states of the country.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestically produced anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine frigates and other military equipment were showcased.
The president, Leslie, was often interrupted by chants of "USA, USA, USA, go fuck yourself" -- a signature chant at state rallies.
The crowd also chanted "Death to Israel."
Reuters said that Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, which is a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 for national security crimes.
They later placed her under house arrest, but she returned to prison in January.
Adelkhah denied these allegations.
A week before Mesaimi was released, his supporters warned that he was at risk of death due to his hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting the mandatory wearing of headscarves.
The French Foreign Ministry responded to Adelkhah's release on Friday, calling for her freedom to be restored, "including if she wishes, she should be allowed to return to France."
“
The 16th China-Japan Energy Saving and Environmental Protection Comprehensive Forum was held in Beijing. He Lifeng attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech - China News
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 11 (Reporter Liu Yazhe) - On February 11, the 16th China-Japan Energy Conservation and Environmental Protection Integrated Forum was held in Beijing in a combination of online and offline modes.
Hu Lifeng, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and director of the National Development and Reform Commission, attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
He Li Feng pointed out that holding this forum is an important measure to implement the consensus reached by President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Fumio Kishida at the G20 Summit in Bangkok and to strengthen green development cooperation between China and Japan.
China will comprehensively implement the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress, accelerate the green transformation of development, deepen environmental pollution prevention and control, comprehensively strengthen resource conservation, actively and prudently promote carbon peaking and carbon neutrality, and promote decarbonization, pollution reduction, greening, and growth in a coordinated manner, and promote ecological priority, resource conservation, and low-carbon and green development.
China is willing to work with Japan to continue deepening cooperation in green and low-carbon industries, technology cooperation, policy dialogue and people-to-people exchanges, and promote the green development cooperation between the two countries to a new level.
Japanese Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry Hiroshige Sekimoto attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
The forum was jointly organized by the National Development and Reform Commission of China, the Ministry of Commerce of China and the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry of Japan, and the Japan-China Economic Association. It included a main forum and four sub-forums on energy efficiency, electric vehicles, automation, hydrogen energy, and long-term trade between China and Japan.
Representatives from the governments, enterprises, and institutions of China and Japan exchanged views.
Hunan Questions and Answers: How to View the Employment Data in the United States in January and the Future Trend - Economic Observer - A Professional Financial News Website
Q: How does Qian Yuan Investment view the January non-agricultural employment data in the United States, which exceeded expectations, and the future trend?
A: On February 3, the US Department of Labor announced the non-farm employment data in January 2023, with 51.7 thousand new non-farm employment, which is significantly higher than the market expectation of 18.9 thousand; the unemployment rate fell to 3.4%, the lowest in nearly 50 years; the hourly wage growth rate was 4.4% year-on-year and 0.3% month-on-month, with slight slowdown.
In terms of the total amount, there are many one-time and technical factors that affect the data, such as the return to work of teachers on strike, the revision of the survey and statistical scope, and the update of the seasonal factor. It is expected that there will be some adjustments in the future (refer to the new non-farm payrolls added in January 2022, which were revised from 50.4 thousand to 36.4 thousand); non-farm employment is not as strong as the data shows.
In terms of structure, the impact of layoffs on high-tech enterprises is still significant, but the proportion is relatively low; the newly added employment in high-contact service industries such as leisure hotels, education and health care has rebounded significantly, and the data shows that the labor shortage in the service industry still exists.
Combined with the same large excess of service industry PMI, the recovery of job vacancies and labor shortage data, and the strong consumer credit data, we judge that the US service industry has undergone rapid recovery after extreme weather and holidays.
We believe that the tightness of the U.S. labor market will be difficult to improve without a recession.
At present, the supply gap of the US labor market is still more than 5 million, and the labor participation rate is rising slowly, especially the labor participation rate of 25-54-year-olds has reached the peak before the epidemic.
In addition, the strong consumption demand will further delay the impact of contractionary policies on the employment market, due to the excess savings and strong consumption credit of American residents.
The tight labor market in the US will be the bottom color of the US economy in 2023.
The combination of the near-ending of the tightening cycle and the repeated fluctuation of inflation expectations is not optimistic about the continuous decline of wage growth.
Prior to the release of the data, the US stock, bond and foreign exchange markets were overly optimistic about the path of interest rate hikes by the Federal Reserve.
As inflation data continued to improve, the Fed maintained a balance between shortening the pace of interest rate hikes and preserving the fragile balance of market inflation expectations. However, the market ignored the Fed's hawkish statements and expected not only an early end to interest rate hikes but also two rate cuts by the end of the year.
In the situation of tight labor market supply and demand and the unclear impact of tightening policies, we believe that the Fed's guidance on interest rate hikes at the end of the year is relatively reasonable, and the adjustment of extreme market expectations and the congestion of transactions will cause some harm to the market.
Despite this, the stubbornness of wage growth is hard to change in the current trend of rapid decline in inflation. With the M2 data turning negative year-on-year and the gradual improvement of various leading indicators of CPI, the US CPI data has turned to the stage of rapid decline since October. The stubbornness of wage growth will only provide a cushion for future inflation data. The current market expectation is difficult to be proved wrong, and the market may enter a new round of competition after the next inflation data is released.
Shenzhen: Building the first and leading city of extreme speed pioneers in China - China News Service
China News Service, February 11 - According to the "Shenzhen Industry and Information" WeChat public number, the Shenzhen Municipal Industry and Information Bureau recently issued the "Shenzhen Action Plan for the Construction of the Ultra-Fast City".
By the end of 2023, a super broadband network with high speed, large capacity, and low latency will be built, and the network construction goal of "double gigabit, all-optical network, 1 millisecond, and all things connected" will be achieved, and a super-fast vanguard city will be built, ranking first in China and leading the world.
The plan proposes to speed up the upgrade of the gigabit optical network.
By the end of 2023, the proportion of 10G PON ports will reach 100%, and the number of full-light industrial parks (industrial parks) will exceed 100.
The plan requires a comprehensive improvement in the energy efficiency of 5G networks.
Research and formulate Shenzhen 5G network service quality standards, carry out 5G network testing and evaluation, and improve the quality of 5G network services.
Support the operators of basic telecommunications to increase the optimization of 5G networks in key areas and places, and add 10,000 5G base stations throughout the year. The average download speed in the city will reach 500 Mbps, and the upload speed will reach 100 Mbps. The download speed in key areas will reach 1 Gbps, and the upload speed will reach 200 Mbps. The network speed and user experience will be greatly improved.
Build a high-quality wireless local area network at the city level.
To establish a standard for public WLAN services, to promote the upgrade of WLAN in areas with dense population and information consumption needs in all districts of the city, and to provide 1000Mbps access capability.
By leveraging the "Shen i net", the city has built a unified authentication and management platform for public wireless local area networks, which supports "one-time authentication, roaming without awareness, and intelligent switching". The platform supports the operation entities to include the APs (access points) with public service capabilities in the authentication and management platform.
By the end of 2023, the total number of APs to be upgraded will be more than 20,000.
In addition, the plan also proposes to build a high-quality full-light network, construct a multi-level computing power supply system, accelerate the construction of key communication network facilities, and improve the ability of Internet application services.
The Plan clearly states that a cooperative construction of the Internet of Things sensing system should be carried out.
Explore the construction and management mode of urban sensing terminal based on the "open source Huangmeng" operating system, reduce the cost of connection, accelerate the construction of urban-level sensing platform, promote the interconnection of urban IoT platform, various professional IoT platforms, and data in various fields.
To deepen the application of the Internet of Things in urban management, public services, public security, transportation, etc., to expand the fixed sensing of city roads, buildings, public facilities, etc., and to expand the sensing channel of smart networked vehicles, etc.
By the end of 2023, the number of water, electricity, gas, and Internet of Things sensing terminals will exceed 9 million, and more than 20 multi-functional smart pole application demonstration projects will be built.
The plan also noted that efforts will be made to strengthen satellite-ground communication integration applications, lay out low-altitude network infrastructure construction, and promote deep coverage of 5G networks at sea.
At the same time, it will promote the in-depth coverage of 5G network in the sea, build an innovation development ecological environment for the industry, and support the top-level events and activities.
(China News Service)
China’s e-commerce industry is emerging with a “new variable”, how to do live broadcasting in a way that is “content-oriented”?
-China News Service
China News Service, February 11th: New Variables in China's E-commerce Industry - How to Achieve "Content Dominance" in Douyin?
Xia Bin, a reporter from China Finance News
“We entered the e-commerce market late, but from the very beginning, we realized that content is very important if we want to stand out from the thousands of stores.
Fang Fang, a "90s" girl from Guangdong, now runs a health food shop on Douyin, and has made a family-run shop with a history of over 30 years "bloom" online.
Mimic the old Hong Kong film style and add classic Cantonese songs. Open the @Fong Fong one person food TikTok account, and the exquisite videos are new to the eyes.
Recently, at the Douyin e-commerce “Find Peers·Quality Content Sharing Special Session”, Fang Fang attended as a representative of quality creators and shared her experience and feelings about her daily creation.
She said on the spot, "The carefully edited video has attracted a lot of netizens' attention, and many people are interested in the ingredients in my family and want to cook with me. The sales channels have opened up suddenly.
“
Fang Fang used to make videos of cooking soup to make more people love the taste of "old Guangzhou", and sold 300,000 units of nourishing food in a single live broadcast, saving the old store that was on the verge of bankruptcy.
“No content, no e-commerce”, as short videos and live broadcast e-commerce continue to develop, people’s requirements and standards for e-commerce content are entering a new stage.
In the early days of live broadcasting, live broadcast rooms often attracted users with low price discounts, and price advantage seemed to be the only selling point at that time.
In recent years, there have been many phenomenal KOLs, such as Liu Liang Hong and Fan Jia Yuan, as well as many non-mainstream KOLs and merchants who have emerged in the vertical field. They have continuously created high-quality content that matches their brand characteristics, and have improved their long-term operating efficiency.
Gao Yaxuan, the head of the operation of the star author of the video e-commerce of Douyin, introduced that in the past year, 6.27 million creators have turned their content into income through Douyin video e-commerce, and their content creation volume has increased by 252%, and the total sales amount has increased by more than 100%.
“Behind these numbers, we can feel a thriving and vibrant author ecosystem.
Gao Yaxuan said.
The Beijing Normal University Platform for Innovation and Future Media has previously released the ECHI Report on the Health Index of the Content Ecology in the E-commerce Industry, which analyzes the importance of high-quality content from the perspective of data. It uses the index to evaluate the content ecology of 27 mainstream e-commerce platforms in China.
According to the above-mentioned report on the health index of the e-commerce industry content ecology, the top five are TikTok, Kuaishou, Taobao, Pinduoduo, and JD.
The report believes that the e-commerce industry content ecology is a comprehensive concept, which integrates e-commerce and content, but not all content can be integrated with e-commerce. The best PGC (professional production of content) and UGC (user-generated content) are the carriers for the integration of e-commerce and content, and the value of the content platform is higher, the consumption and promotion scenarios are more and more rich, and the possibility of e-commerce integration is also higher, and the commercial value is also stronger. The proportion of public and private integration of e-commerce content production and consumption will gradually increase.
At the scene, Professor Yue Guoming, a professor of the School of Journalism and Communication of Beijing Normal University and the chairman of the China Media Economics and Management Committee, made an analysis and interpretation of the report.
He said that in terms of content value, the e-commerce industry has now transitioned from "consumer accessibility" to "consumer quality", and high-quality, professional, and differentiated content is the "hard currency" of the e-commerce industry.
At the same time, content becomes the fundamental and the handle for the new stage of e-commerce development. PGC (Professional Generated Content) content such as knowledge payment, professional knowledge, KOL (Key Opinion Leader) and so on becomes the standard in e-commerce live broadcast.
Looking ahead to the future development of the e-commerce industry, Yu Guomin put forward two suggestions.
One is to promote the health and overall quality of the e-commerce content ecology from the perspective of improving the content structure, and to build positive content creation and management standards to achieve a healthy system index and dynamic balance of the e-commerce industry content ecology.
Another one is from the external ecological perspective, to achieve the healthy development of the content e-commerce industry and the value co-creation and co-prosperity with the external environment.
In the future, the e-commerce industry needs more support in data and artificial intelligence to make predictions about the future development; in addition, it needs to provide a more standardized and healthy growth space for merchants to achieve value coordination among enterprises, users, products and services in the e-commerce industry, and jointly create a healthy content ecology.
"(" (complete)
The Biden administration will blacklist six Chinese entities suspected of participating in the spy balloon project on Friday (February 10).
The U.S. Department of Commerce said the five Chinese companies and one research institution helped modernize the Chinese military, especially in the aviation and aerospace projects, including flying boats and aircraft.
Companies on the blacklist have a hard time getting U.S. technology exports.
The list is called an “entity list,” and companies that enter it will be unable to purchase technology or goods from US suppliers unless they obtain a special export license from the US Department of Commerce.
The companies listed on the blacklist are: Beijing Nanjiang Sky Space Technology Co., Ltd., China Electronics Science and Technology Group Fourth Eighth Research Institute, Dongguan Lingkong Remote Sensing Technology Co., Ltd., Eagle Gate Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd., Guangzhou Tianhai Xiang Aeronautical Technology Co., Ltd., and Shanxi Eagle Gate Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd.
Prior to this, the White House said it was considering more sweeping measures to "expose and address" China's broader surveillance activities that threaten U.S. national security.
The balloon incident has further strained relations between China and the United States, and US Secretary of State Blinken has canceled his visit to China.
On February 4, the United States shot down a balloon. The Chinese government made a serious representation to the US embassy in China, criticizing the United States for seriously undermining and damaging the efforts and process of stabilizing Sino-US relations.
Based on the existing debris evidence and information from the Chinese military procurement platform, the US government concluded that the manufacturer of the balloon was "directly related to the Chinese People's Liberation Army" and was an approved supplier of the Chinese military.
The spokesperson of the Chinese Foreign Ministry Mao Ning said at a press conference on Friday that China has explained the situation and clarified its position on the accidental entry of a Chinese unmanned aerial vehicle into the airspace of the United States due to force majeure.
According to the website of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, she added that the relevant resolution of the US Congress was purely political manipulation and fabrication.
China is strongly dissatisfied and resolutely opposes this.
The assistant secretary for export enforcement at the U.S. Department of Commerce, Matthew Axelrod, said, “Today’s action demonstrates our collective efforts to identify and disrupt China’s use of spy balloons that have violated the airspace of the United States and more than 40 countries.
“
Reuters reported that an employee of Guangzhou Tianhe Aviation Technology Co., Ltd. Said he was not aware of the sanctions and refused to comment further.
China's embassy in the United States and the Chinese Foreign Ministry have not commented on the information.
(Reuters, etc.)
