At present, there is no official feedback channel for Amazon, so we can only leave feedback in the product reviews.
1. On March 29, I purchased the book for 31 yuan through pre-order, and it showed that it would be pushed to my device on March 31. At this time, I could not preview the book on Amazon's official website (because it had not been published yet);
The book sent to the device on March 31 was blank, with only "Please look forward to it", and the electronic version of the book on Amazon was reduced to 18 yuan.
3. I have repeatedly tried to delete the blank books that were downloaded on the device, and then synchronize it again, but I can't get the electronic version of "The Nature of Business" that contains actual content, but I can see that Amazon's official website can preview the book.
I have a few thoughts at the moment.
1. The problem of price is not the most important. The key is how to replace the blank books on kindle with books with actual content now. It is not always "please wait" when downloading.
2. After pre-ordering the book, I will not buy it again, because if the book is delayed, I will download a book with empty content, and the procedures are very complicated.
3. I hope Amazon provides a normal channel to report such issues; when there is any doubt about downloading or using e-books, one can have an outlet to feedback (e.g., through tickets or online customer service). This can be similar to how Microsoft’s official store handles it.
Lonely little lion
When I got the book, I thought it would be as simple as Lost City, but there are still a lot of words!
I read it three times to the kids, a lion who can shoot, a lion who likes to drink juice-flavored gum.
When I saw the scene of the lion eating the hunter, I felt a little uncomfortable, and modern city people can’t accept such an arrangement of being eaten by animals.
In the end, the little lion, who had succeeded in human society, was lost, and he was no longer a complete lion or a complete human.
Finally, only the silhouette of the little lion is left, and I don't know where he went.
Maybe years later, the image of the little lion will remain in the memory of the grown-up little friend, and will be recalled by chance one day, perhaps touching or inspiring her.
