2 Then in the middle, you contact the customer service personnel, and they will tell you that this problem will be handled by a specialist, and they will inform you of the result.
You can never get in touch with this commissioner, you don't know her work number, and there is no direct contact phone number, it's just that you can't get in touch with her, only she can contact you.
The tragedy is that I waited for nearly 3 days, and the specialist called me, but I left my phone for a while, and I didn't get the call from the specialist.
I waited for two hours without getting that specialist's call; I then contacted Amazon customer service and sent an email to them asking her to call me back.
I have not received any response from Amazon about the processing of the defective coffee machine I received in the past three days.
The products of Amazon in the United States are fine, but the shopping method of overseas shopping is good, but the service of BuyUSA is much worse than that of Amazon.
Six is not enough for me; I can only continue to wait...
Not really recommending it.
I read this a long time ago, and I just happened to come across it and write a review.
This book is not so much a collection of short stories as it is a collection of fragments of life about love.
The tone of the book is very plain, it is the kind of plain tone that is as plain as water, the use of words and phrases is to the extreme in pursuit of simplicity, and the plot is as plain as the streets in the afternoon of a summer day.
Each short story is a fragment of a moment in ordinary life, without a beginning or an end.
The songs were eventually collected together and titled "What We Talk About When We Talk About Love".
I think this collection of short stories, and its title, is a kind of performance art. The author wants to express that love is not just the joys and sorrows of life on stage, but also the urban legend of being worn out and shabby; it is not just the sticky and glue-like relationship between you and me, but also the life that is as plain as water, the monotonous and tasteless daily life, and the helplessness and escape from reality, as well as the confusion about the future.
Reading this book, you may recall the quarrelling couple around you, the boring marriage of the acquaintance, and the unpleasant relationship.
This is the reason why I do not recommend reading it. From the aesthetic point of view, the writing and plot of the book are tasteless, unless you live in a world of turbulent waves or a world of sweetness like living in a candy castle. Otherwise, you will feel that it is strange and boring to read it.
And in terms of depth of thought, everyday situations do not surprise or expand one’s mind and perspective (this is unlike in Gabriel Garcia Marquez’s Love in the Time of Cholera), while brief episodes fail to address any issues, such as what kind of mistake led to the failure of love?
What causes the breakdown of the protagonist's marriage?
So I don't recommend reading this book, whether you read it or not doesn't matter much.
The author's ideas are expressed more through techniques and forms rather than story plots, which is also the reason why the reading experience of this book is not good.
